#libfortuna

This library uses code from the PostgreSQL database project.
http://www.postgres.org/

The original source location (in the postgres source tree) is
contrib/pgcrypto. Also, parts of src/include/postgres.h and 
src/include/c.h

Waitman Gobble <waitman@waitman.net> 2013-07-12

Documentation and more information at the following URL:
http://www.crxwg.com/fortuna/bin/libfortuna.html


RISC OS
-------

The library can be built as an exported library for RISC OS (32-bit and
64-bit). Build it from the RISCOS directory with 'riscos-amu export'; this
produces the headers and library as Fortuna in the exported libraries. The
test command can be built with 'riscos-amu -f MakefileTest,fe1' and run with
'riscos-run aif32.FortunaTest'.

* The header 'c.h' is named 'fortuna_c.h', as the RISC OS C compiler cannot
  include a file called 'c.h'.
* Entropy is read from the CryptRandom module. If that is not available, the
  library falls back to the timers and pointer state, which is a weak source.
* On 32-bit systems, SHA-384 and SHA-512 use pairs of 32-bit values, as there
  is no 64-bit integer type.
* The library uses vsnprintf, which is not in the default (noc99) C library
  stubs. Programs which link against the library must set CLIBTYPE = generic.
